        "problem": "Calculate $-A+2B$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-1$ and each entry of $B$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A+2B & =(-1)[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot 3 & (-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+0 & -1+(-4) \\\\ -1+(-4) & 0+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
